==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*3 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Metal One Horn]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*5 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Koronium]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**6 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**10 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
**1 [[Mr. Mole]] spawns.
**10 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You should try to use [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] to control the non-[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can be used here to get rid of the Kang Roos if they start stacking. For Koronium, you should bring an [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area]] [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critter]] like [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]], especially if the Metal One Horns stack.

For 4 crowns, since there're no good Critter that is immune to or can survive Koronium's [[Wave Attack]]s without getting juggled, you can brute-force through his whole 150 health using spam and/or [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|wave-immune]] attackers such as [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] to steadily chew through it.

If you have [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]] or [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]], this stage becomes a cakewalk. Simply deploy E. Kubilan at the right time to easily take out Koronium, or lure the enemies to the [[Cat Base]] and deploy Yaminora with some Critters.

==Trivia==
*Burning Blue may be named for the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]]'s blue [[Surge Attack]]s.

